  "name": "r9-vectors-recovery",
  "note": "Recovery Kit v2 (Astation-owned): one 256-bit secret R. sign_seed = HKDF-SHA256(salt empty, ikm R, info \"atem-recovery-sign-v1\", 32) is an Ed25519 seed; its public key is the recovery_key (genesis, or set_recovery_key). The kit's X25519 key is the same key in Montgomery form (secret SHA-512(sign_seed)[0..32], public = Montgomery(recovery_key)). K backup atem-k-backup-v2 = RFC 9180 base mode, DHKEM(X25519, HKDF-SHA256), HKDF-SHA256, ChaCha20-Poly1305, to that X25519 public key, info = enc([\"atem-k-backup-v2\", account_id, genesis_hash(32), u64(blob_version), jcs(kids), recovery_key pub(32)]), empty AAD, plaintext jcs({keys}); the sender's ephemeral is DeriveKeyPair(ikmE). backup_hash = hex(SHA-256(enc([\"atem-k-backup-hash-v1\", jcs(envelope)]))), recorded by the k_backup log entry. The kit also carries account_id and genesis_hash, bound by kit_tag (kit, kit_2.kit); a restore trusts only a log whose genesis is the kit's (substitute_chain is refused).",
